    "focal_pair": {
      "annotated_sentence_text": "[Turn 2 USER]\ne010\tI do not think Tomas wants to resolve it cosmetically.\ne011\tHe is usually the one who includes awkward stories.\ne012\tI am the person who keeps building the catalog and saying we need better dates and names.\ne013\tHe thinks my standard of organization is a way of postponing anything public until nobody is interested.\ne014\tThat hurts because there is some truth in it.\ne015\tBut when he tells stories confidently, relatives often remember them differently.\n[Turn 2 ASSISTANT]\ne016\tThen the difference may be less honesty versus polish and more tolerance for incomplete evidence.\ne017\tYour cataloging protects traceability; his storytelling keeps the material connected to living attention.\ne018\tAn exhibition could show conflicting memories rather than choose among them, although that approach can become a curatorial device that feels cleverer than the family experience.\ne019\tIt would help to identify which disagreements are enriching and which could make someone feel misrepresented.",
